      "blurb": "The biceps attaches just below the front of the elbow. Heavy lifting, pulling, or repeated turning of the forearm palm-up can overload the tendon there, giving pain in the elbow crease. A sudden pop with bruising or a bulge in the upper arm is different: that can be a tear, which needs a doctor the same day.",
