      "blurb": "A knock or a fall can bruise the skin, muscle and bone surface around the elbow. It is sore, may swell and bruise, and is tender to lean on. When the elbow still straightens fully and the bony points are not very sore to press, a break is unlikely. Most bruises settle over 1 to 3 weeks, and gentle movement from early on may help prevent stiffness.",
