      "blurb": "A nerve that runs through the muscles at the top of the forearm can be squeezed where it passes a few finger-widths below the outer elbow. It gives a deep, tiring ache in the forearm rather than pain on the bony bump, and usually no numbness. It often sits alongside tennis elbow and is easy to mistake for it.",
