      "blurb": "After a broken bone in the hand or a finger, or an operation such as a tendon repair, the hand needs protecting while it heals, and the fingers stiffen quickly. Following your fracture clinic's or surgeon's plan, with a splint and carefully chosen exercises at each stage, can help bring back a good fist and grip. Recovery usually takes a few months.",
