      "blurb": "A snap or clunk you can feel, see or hear as the hip moves. On the outside of the hip, a band of tissue flicks over the bony point; at the front, the hip flexor tendon flicks over the bone underneath. It is common in dancers, gymnasts and runners, is often painless and harmless, and when it is sore most people settle with changes to training and a targeted exercise plan.",
