      "name": "Recovering from a knee cartilage injury, bone bruise or OCD",
      "clin": "Traumatic chondral or osteochondral lesion, bone contusion, or osteochondritis dissecans of the knee, after diagnosis",
      "blurb": "The smooth cartilage on the ends of the knee bones can be injured in a twist, a landing or a kneecap dislocation, sometimes with a small piece of the bone beneath it, and a bone bruise is swelling in the bone just under the joint surface. In osteochondritis dissecans (OCD), seen mostly in active teenagers, a small patch of bone under the cartilage weakens. Once a doctor has checked it, rehabilitation within their plan helps many people get back to sport and activity; bone bruises usually settle within 2 to 4 months.",
