      "blurb": "A skin nerve runs down the inside of the knee to the inner shin. It can be irritated by knee surgery, a knock, or pressure, giving a burning, tingling, or numb patch on the inner or front of the knee, or the inner shin. It is a feeling nerve only, so the leg is not weak. Numbness beside a knee scar is common, and the patch usually shrinks over the following year.",
