      "blurb": "Axial spondyloarthritis is a form of inflammatory arthritis that mainly affects the spine and the sacroiliac joints at the base of the back. Unlike the common \"mechanical\" back pain that follows a lift or a long day, the pain and stiffness come from inflammation, so they are worst after rest and sleep and better once you get moving. Ankylosing spondylitis is the name used when the changes can be seen on an X-ray. It is a long-term condition, but it is well understood and treatable: regular exercise and, where needed, medication from a rheumatologist help most people stay active, flexible and working.",
