      "blurb": "Spondylolisthesis means one of the bones in the lower back sits a little forward of the bone below it. In younger adults this usually follows a small stress crack in a part of the bone called the pars, often from years of arching sports. From about 50 onwards it usually comes from gradual change in the discs and small joints, which lets the bone shift. Most slips are small and the spine stays stable: they are often found on scans in people with no pain at all, and a slip does not mean your back is fragile or \"out of place\". Many people do well with a plan that builds strength and confidence in the back and hips.",
