      "name": "Sensitive nerve in the arm (neural mechanosensitivity)",
      "clin": "Upper-limb neural mechanosensitivity (nerve-related neck and arm pain; median, ulnar or radial nerve irritation or entrapment)",
      "blurb": "Nerves run from the neck to the fingers and have to slide and stretch every time you move your arm and neck. Sometimes a nerve becomes more sensitive to that stretch or to pressure, often after a period of irritation at the neck, shoulder, elbow or wrist, and positions that put it on stretch can then bring on ache, tingling or burning along the arm. A sensitive nerve is usually not a damaged nerve: nerves have a good blood supply and adapt well, and gentle movements that help them glide, together with changes to the positions that irritate them, can help them settle.",
