        "Wrist and hand interface (\"PhysioChandra WristHand Conditions.docx\" form 19, v1.0, 20 Oct 2026): carpal tunnel and Guyon's canal as interfaces; double crush with the neck; sliders before tensioners (Coppieters and Butler 2008); often emerges during wrist-fracture or carpal tunnel rehab; PRWHE. The form's CPG citation for nerve gliding in CTS is wrong (JOSPT grade D)."
