      "blurb": "The labrum is a rim of firm tissue that deepens the shoulder socket. It can be irritated or torn by repeated throwing or overhead sport, a fall onto an outstretched arm, or a dislocation, giving a deep pain with clicking or catching, often with the arm overhead. Many labral tears, including SLAP tears, settle with rehabilitation, and surgery is not always needed.",
