      "blurb": "The ulnar nerve passes through a small tunnel at the base of the palm on the little-finger side. Long spells of pressure there, such as leaning on handlebars when cycling or pressing on a tool handle, can irritate it, giving tingling in the little and ring fingers. Unlike the same nerve pressed at the elbow, the back of the hand usually still feels normal.",
